<?xml version='1.0' standalone='yes'?>
<!DOCTYPE PLUGIN [
  <!ENTITY name      "wireview-hwmon">
  <!ENTITY author    "emaspa">
  <!ENTITY version   "0.16">
  <!ENTITY repo      "https://github.com/emaspa/wireview-hwmon-unraid">
  <!ENTITY pluginURL "&repo;/raw/main/wireview-hwmon.plg">
  <!ENTITY support   "https://forums.unraid.net/topic/197481-plugin-support-wireview-pro-ii-gpu-power-monitor-wireview-hwmon/">
  <!ENTITY launch    "Utilities/WireviewHwmon">
]>

<PLUGIN name="&name;" author="&author;" version="&version;"
  pluginURL="&pluginURL;" support="&support;" launch="&launch;"
  icon="bolt" min="7.2.0">

  <CHANGES>
## 0.16
- Choose what the dashboard tile shows. Settings > Utilities > WireView
  Pro II has a new Dashboard Tile section: tick the readings to list, pick
  what the header shows next to the status orb, and set the refresh
  interval. The header can show total power, total current, average
  voltage, hottest temperature or energy. Saved on the flash drive.
- The tile shows the energy used since the daemon started, names the
  faults instead of showing a hex mask, and turns a pin, total or
  temperature red when its alarm is set. Fault notifications name the
  faults too.
- Packages for Unraid 7.2.5, 7.2.6, 7.2.7, 7.2.8 and 7.4.0-beta.3, with
  kernels 6.12.85, 6.12.87, 6.12.90, 6.12.98 and 6.18.52. Those releases
  had no package before and the install failed with "Failed to download".
- Update to wireview-hwmon 1.7.1: Noctua Edition support, bundled
  firmware build 20260902_0741, energy counter and alarm attributes in
  hwmon, a 3 second limit on LAN requests, and the fan duty moved from
  fan1_input to pwm1. wireviewctl flash now refuses an older image, an
  image for another product, and the build the device already runs.
- The config editor offers the 2.8 s and 5.7 s averaging windows on
  firmware v05.
- wireviewd and wireviewctl are now linked against musl. A static glibc
  build loads the host's name service libraries and can crash when the
  host glibc differs from the build one.
- The serial port and /dev/wireview-hwmon are no longer world-writable.

## 0.15.1
- Fix the kernel module failing to load on Unraid 7.3.2: no pre-configured
  kernel source existed yet for kernel 6.18.38, and the build fell back to a
  generic config that produced an incompatible module. The build now uses
  the kernel config Unraid ships inside its own release image, and refuses
  to package a module whose version magic does not match the target kernel.
  Reinstall/update the plugin to get the working 7.3.2 package.

## 0.15
- Update to wireview-hwmon 1.5.0.
- Firmware flashing from the terminal: new "wireviewctl flash" command updates
  the device firmware over DFU. The package now bundles the official firmware
  image (v05) and a static dfu-util, so "wireviewctl flash -y" is a complete
  update with no extra downloads - and it can recover a device already stuck
  in bootloader mode. Unofficial tool: flash at your own risk.
- Serial handover protocol: the desktop app (v1.2.0.0) can borrow the USB
  port through the daemon for device log reads, display theme uploads, and
  firmware flashing, then polling resumes automatically.
- Add support for Unraid 7.3.2 (kernel 6.18.38-Unraid).

## 0.14
- Update to wireview-hwmon 1.4.1: fix phantom fault alerts. The daemon now
  discards corrupt (desynced) serial frames via padding/fan-duty sanity
  checks and debounces fault bits across two consecutive frames, so the
  fault monitor and remote viewers no longer alert on garbage frames.
  Suppressed frames are audit-logged.

## 0.13
- Fix saved Network (LAN) values coming back empty: the Unraid webGui appends
  a csrf_token suffix to every AJAX POST body, corrupting the JSON payload, so
  0.12 saved defaults (empty secret/hosts) while reporting success. The
  handlers now strip the appended token before parsing, and reject an
  unparseable body instead of writing defaults. Re-save your settings once
  after updating.

## 0.12
- Fix all settings/config writes from the web UI (root cause found): Unraid's
  CSRF guard silently discards any POST without a csrf_token - and the
  plugin's JSON requests never carried one. All requests now send the
  X-CSRF-Token header. This fixes saving Network (LAN) settings AND the
  device config editor / NVM / clear-faults buttons.

## 0.11
- Rewrite the Network (LAN) settings handler so saving works reliably - verified
  to write the config and always return proper JSON (the 0.7-0.10 attempts left
  the endpoint returning an empty response). If a prior version misbehaved,
  remove and reinstall the plugin for a clean file.

## 0.10
- Really fix saving Network (LAN) settings. The save returned an empty HTTP 200
  body - `fastcgi_finish_request()` (added in 0.8) closed the connection before
  Unraid's output buffer flushed - so the browser couldn't parse the response
  and showed a failure even though the write succeeded. The handler now returns
  the JSON normally and restarts the daemon fully detached.

## 0.9
- Actually fix saving Network (LAN) settings: create the flash config dir
  `/boot/config/plugins/wireview-hwmon` on install (it never existed, so the
  save failed to write it), and stop a leaked PHP warning from corrupting the
  JSON response (which had masked the real error as a generic failure).

## 0.8
- Fix "Failed to save network settings" under Network (LAN): the save now
  returns immediately and restarts the daemon in the background, instead of
  blocking on a full daemon/module restart that timed out the request.

## 0.7
- Update to wireview-hwmon 1.4.0 (LAN monitoring)
- New "Network (LAN)" settings: publish this server on the LAN
  (GET /sensors), authenticated remote writes/config via a network secret,
  configurable port, and audit-log retention - persisted to the flash drive
- Remote-host list for the wireviewctl top monitor

## 0.6
- Add support for Unraid 7.3.1 (kernel 6.18.33-Unraid)
- Add support for current Unraid 7.3.0 (kernel 6.18.29-Unraid)
- Rebuild package for Unraid 7.2.x (kernel 6.12.54-Unraid)

## 0.5
- Add support for firmware v4 config version 2
- Color pickers for primary, secondary, highlight, and background colors
- Default screen and display inversion settings
- Fix config size auto-detection

## 0.4
- Initial release
- Kernel module, daemon, and CLI tool for WireView Pro II
- Unraid web GUI with live sensor display
  </CHANGES>

  <!-- Determine kernel version and download matching package -->
  <FILE Run="/bin/bash">
  <INLINE>
#!/bin/bash
PLUGIN="&name;"
REPO="&repo;"
VERSION="&version;"
KVER=$(uname -r)

echo "--- Installing ${PLUGIN} v${VERSION} for kernel ${KVER} ---"

# Download the matching package from GitHub Releases
PKG_URL="${REPO}/releases/download/v${VERSION}/${PLUGIN}-${VERSION}-x86_64-${KVER}.txz"
PKG_FILE="/tmp/${PLUGIN}.txz"

echo "Downloading ${PKG_URL}..."
wget -q -O "${PKG_FILE}" "${PKG_URL}"
if [ $? -ne 0 ]; then
  echo "ERROR: Failed to download package for kernel ${KVER}."
  echo "Your Unraid kernel version may not be supported yet."
  echo "Check ${REPO}/releases for available packages."
  rm -f "${PKG_FILE}"
  exit 1
fi

# Install the Slackware package
installpkg "${PKG_FILE}"
rm -f "${PKG_FILE}"

# Persistent config dir on the flash drive. LAN/network settings are saved here
# by the webGui; create it as root at install time since the webGui PHP context
# can't reliably create dirs under /boot itself.
mkdir -p /boot/config/plugins/${PLUGIN}

# Rebuild module dependency list
depmod -a

# Load kernel module
modprobe wireview_hwmon || {
  echo "Recent kernel log:"
  dmesg | tail -5
  echo "WARNING: Could not load wireview_hwmon module."
  echo "It will be loaded when the daemon starts."
}

# Reload udev rules
udevadm control --reload-rules 2>/dev/null
udevadm trigger 2>/dev/null

# Start the daemon
if [ -x /etc/rc.d/rc.wireviewd ]; then
  /etc/rc.d/rc.wireviewd start
fi

echo "--- ${PLUGIN} installed successfully ---"
  </INLINE>
  </FILE>

  <!-- Removal script -->
  <FILE Run="/bin/bash" Method="remove">
  <INLINE>
#!/bin/bash
PLUGIN="&name;"

echo "--- Removing ${PLUGIN} ---"

# Stop the daemon
if [ -x /etc/rc.d/rc.wireviewd ]; then
  /etc/rc.d/rc.wireviewd stop
fi

# Unload kernel module
rmmod wireview_hwmon 2>/dev/null

# Remove the Slackware package
removepkg "${PLUGIN}" 2>/dev/null

# Rebuild module dependency list
depmod -a

# Reload udev rules
udevadm control --reload-rules 2>/dev/null
udevadm trigger 2>/dev/null

# Clean up plugin config directory
rm -rf /boot/config/plugins/${PLUGIN}

echo "--- ${PLUGIN} removed ---"
  </INLINE>
  </FILE>

</PLUGIN>
